{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_177fd386b796e3afa2f39c569f20c5858d4462abeb3c15d04ebf2164b7b91e2f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the monorepo offers make setup, check-test, check, and test targets, plus check-py/test-py for Python; TypeScript and Go projects are expected to define their own commands in package.json and Makefiles."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1c49c1fae4258d95de0abc4cf4dd6d9fd749464a8b458b38c16d949673c7ce41"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: MCP servers launched by Claude Code sessions are passed HUMANLAYER_DAEMON_SOCKET so they connect to the daemon instance that launched them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22c39c780ce9b703a46c1130f08bc00dc043a2b6045866a0730dfca25dc94511"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: DEVELOPMENT.md describes parallel 'nightly' (stable) and 'dev' (testing) environments so daemon or WUI changes can be tested without restarting the daemon and breaking active Claude sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_31799fa410e759f6199b6b0ff2205071c9ed4abfdde7bebb64715a0a44b43f79"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the daemon and WUI respect HUMANLAYER_DAEMON_SOCKET, HUMANLAYER_DATABASE_PATH, and HUMANLAYER_DAEMON_VERSION_OVERRIDE environment variables, with the socket variable defaulting to ~/.humanlayer/daemon.sock."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a7214538f8b3ea1fab2ee34bca831fff49d4d695f35fe8adf9d8aeb4da12297e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: make targets such as daemon-nightly, wui-nightly, daemon-dev, wui-dev, copy-db-to-dev, cleanup-dev, and dev-status build and run each environment; make daemon-dev starts with a fresh database copy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d11c603c3825dd625f1a1801c7ae074377531796d42c121cb5afcdc07d577f43"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the two environments use separate Unix sockets (daemon.sock vs daemon-dev.sock) and separate databases (daemon.db vs timestamped dev DBs) to prevent accidental cross-connections."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fbba4f4433e8a236e51d28882eb61c2ff5fd51be933692d3957b512656b15b26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: npx humanlayer launch accepts a custom daemon socket via a --daemon-socket flag, the HUMANLAYER_DAEMON_SOCKET environment variable, or a daemon_socket entry in humanlayer.json."}],"claim_ids":["clm_177fd386b796e3afa2f39c569f20c5858d4462abeb3c15d04ebf2164b7b91e2f","clm_1c49c1fae4258d95de0abc4cf4dd6d9fd749464a8b458b38c16d949673c7ce41","clm_22c39c780ce9b703a46c1130f08bc00dc043a2b6045866a0730dfca25dc94511","clm_31799fa410e759f6199b6b0ff2205071c9ed4abfdde7bebb64715a0a44b43f79","clm_a7214538f8b3ea1fab2ee34bca831fff49d4d695f35fe8adf9d8aeb4da12297e","clm_d11c603c3825dd625f1a1801c7ae074377531796d42c121cb5afcdc07d577f43","clm_fbba4f4433e8a236e51d28882eb61c2ff5fd51be933692d3957b512656b15b26"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_f17f8df65a784acd8e20fdd27adb5041","id":"pg_211060065895576696dffd34c2d4abba","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/humanlayer-humanlayer-development-md-99abe673498c-fd34c2d4abba.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_814a7c129471583aa9b8550d44f0814e"],"title":"humanlayer/humanlayer/DEVELOPMENT.md @ 99abe673498c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f17f8df65a784acd8e20fdd27adb5041"}
